  "description": "Single 15 MW gas turbine backed by 6 MW solar and an 8 MW / 4 MWh grid-forming BESS. GPU/data traffic starts at 200 nodes (2.10 MW gross compute) and ramps to 800 nodes (8.41 MW gross compute) over 30 minutes — a 300% increase (4×). Solar (anchored at San Diego solar noon, 88% irradiance) delivers a steady ~5.28 MW offset throughout the run. The turbine is idle at t=0 while solar covers the full baseline load; it begins contributing as traffic waves arrive. By peak (t≈1500 s) the turbine covers the ~3.13 MW net demand gap that solar cannot. BESS bridges staging gaps on each job-wave STARTING event (30 s advance warning). No gen-trip events — this is a clean ramp demonstration, not a contingency drill.",

